# The sensitive surfaces below carry owners
# again. The file used to be empty ("disabled to prevent PR deadlock"), which
# left workflows, .quality, baselines, deny.toml and Cargo.toml with no review
# owner at all - the baseline rule was convention plus ci-workflow-guards
# only. Coverage is scoped to the surfaces whose loosening is invisible in
# code review; everything else stays ownerless so routine PRs do not deadlock.
# Bot PRs (dependabot) touch these paths when they edit workflows or the
# manifests - those PRs need a human look by design; the grouping and
# open-pull-requests-limit in dependabot.yml keep the volume reviewable.
#
# Owners are the repository owner (this is a single-maintainer repository;
# the previous note's "assign to teams" has no team to assign to here).

# CI and its guardrails: every workflow, the lint/deny tables and the
# quality gates.
/.github/workflows/ @lubosruler
/.quality/ @lubosruler
/.github/clippy-extra-baseline.txt @lubosruler
/.github/codeql/ @lubosruler
/codeql/ @lubosruler

# Supply-chain and policy manifests: a loosened deny or audit table is
# invisible in a code diff.
/budzero/deny.toml @lubosruler
/.cargo/audit.toml @lubosruler
/supply-chain/ @lubosruler
/audits.toml @lubosruler
/.github/dependabot.yml @lubosruler

# The dependency surface itself: manifest changes route to the same owner.
/Cargo.toml @lubosruler
/Cargo.lock @lubosruler
